[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1336","stub":{"id":"1336","section":"Howe Road to Mill Road","altname":"","river":"Lake Ozonia Outlet","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"362","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"111851","location":{"latitude":"44.6632995605469","longitude":"-74.5899963378906"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117123","location":{"latitude":"44.6876983642578","longitude":"-74.6120986938477"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"3","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"1336","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"I have only run this once, so take any statements with a grain of salt. We ran it at 1100 cfs on the St. Regis Gauge, and it was a great level.\n\nPut-in can be a problem. We found a trail from Howe Rd. that brought us into the river about 1 mile upstream of the start of the whitewater, but I doubt this is an 'sanctioned' put-in. Other than searching for unposted trails along Howe Rd., or asking permission, other options are to put in way upstream as mentioned in 'New York Exposed', or use Dexter Lake Outlet, as mentioned in the below comment.\n\nThe rapids start about 1 mile above the route 458 bridge. Straightforward, continuous, boat scoutable rapids to just above the 458 bridge. Most interesting stuff starts about 200 yards above the bridge. Scout on river right to keep out of people's yards. Below the bridge (just out of sight if you are standing on the bridge) is an interesting drop that is worth a look, Scout on river right. Below this, there is one more fun drop/slide, then river starts to ease off as it joins the St. Regis.\n\nTake out is 0.7 miles downstream on the St. Regis River, at the Mill Rd. bridge.","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"2.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"1336","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2500"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"WEST BRANCH ST. REGIS RIVER NEAR PARISHVILLE NY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"04268800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"362","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.99","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"44.59875","longitude":"-74.7372222"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/04268800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/04268800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nToo Low to Boat (L0-L9): 0 - 800 cfs  Comment: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 800 - 2500 cfs  Comment: The upper limit of this range is a rough guess, based on historical data for this gauge.\nToo High to Boat (H0-H9): 2501 - 5000 cfs  Comment: Estimated\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":"This is a gauge on a nearby stream; use it with caution.","status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"362","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["111851","117123"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-74.58989831859321,44.66324665